//? Title: Never Give Up-style episodic novelty
//? Lang: en

> Never Give Up-style episodic novelty

An [inverse-dynamics encoder|curiosity_model.mepml] learns state features
from replay. The agent snapshots all features at each episode boundary
so distances within an episode use one representation. Memory starts
with the initial state and records every successor, including repeats.

The bonus uses up to five nearest visits in that memory. Squared
distances are divided by their running mean across episodes, then
reduced by a small clustering threshold. A sum of kernel similarities
estimates density, and its inverse square root gives the novelty bonus.
This example isolates the episodic component of Never Give Up.

The [shared grid schedule|exploration_grid.mepml] compares three matched
control and novelty runs. The plot tracks coverage across seeds. The
table also reports task success and inverse-action accuracy on replay.

[Badia et al. (2020), Never Give Up|https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06038]

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/never_give_up.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;
  namespace r=dm::rl;
  const auto pack=[](std::span<const std::array<int,3>> batch) {
    std::vector<int> values;
    for (const auto& row:batch) values.insert(values.end(),row.begin(),row.end());
    return n::from_vector(values,{std::ssize(batch),3});
  };
  std::vector<double> control,ngu;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| Seed | Mode | Visited | Training goals | Greedy success | Inverse accuracy |\n"
             "|---:|:---|---:|---:|:---|---:|\n");
  for (const auto seed:{43602u,43603u,43604u}) {
    const auto [path,reward,visited,goals,success]=r::sparse_grid_experiment(seed);
    control.push_back(visited);
    std::print("| {} | Control | {} | {} | {} | |\n",seed,visited,goals,success);
    n::save_npz(std::format("build/{}_control.npz",seed),{{"transitions",path},{"bonus",reward}});

    r::IntrinsicCuriosity model(49,4,12,24,0.);
    r::EpisodicNovelty novelty;
    std::vector<int> states(49);
    std::iota(states.begin(),states.end(),0);
    const auto ids=n::from_vector(states);
    std::vector<n::Tensor> snapshots;
    const auto [rows,bonus,coverage,hits,solved]=r::sparse_grid_experiment(seed,
        [&](const auto& step) {
          return static_cast<float>(novelty.observe(step[2]));
        },
        [&](const auto batch) { model.train(pack(batch)); },
        [&] {
          snapshots.push_back(model.embed(ids));
          novelty.reset(snapshots.back());
        });
    ngu.push_back(coverage);
    const auto [error,prediction,target,logits]=model.evaluate(rows);
    const auto actions=n::slice(rows,{0,1},{rows.size(0),1}).to_vector<int>();
    const auto guesses=n::argmax(logits,1).to_vector<int>();
    int correct=0;
    for (std::size_t i=0;i<actions.size();++i) correct+=actions[i]==guesses[i];
    std::print("| {} | NGU-style | {} | {} | {} | {:.3f} |\n",
               seed,coverage,hits,solved,double(correct)/actions.size());
    n::save_npz(std::format("build/{}_ngu.npz",seed),{{"transitions",rows},{"bonus",bonus},
        {"final_error",error},{"prediction",prediction},{"features",target},{"inverse_logits",logits},
        {"episode_embeddings",n::stack(snapshots)}});
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points({43602,43603,43604},control,"Task reward only",{217,96,26},7)
      .points({43602,43603,43604},ngu,"With episodic novelty",{37,99,235},7)
      .title("Sparse-grid exploration coverage").x_label("Seed").y_label("Unique cells visited")
      .ylim(0,49).size(820,460).save_svg("build/never_give_up.svg");
}
```
